// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 14-control-flow
// facility: rule.control.frame-references (Handing over on assignment, D-0300); conf.ref-copy-source-reassigned-in-loop
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (dynamic)
//
// `r1 = r2` gives `r1` a fact through `r2`'s referent; `r2 = &x` then
// points `r2` elsewhere, and the fact `r1` held through the old referent is
// handed to what `r2` held (D-0300), as it is when `r2` ends. On the second
// pass `r1` holds what `r2` was pointed at, `x`, so the write to `x` after
// the loop meets `r1`'s path. Before D-0300 the fact was cleared with
// `r2`'s assignment, the program was decided, and `cobc` wrote with no check.

import std;

fn main()
{
    i32 x = 1;
    i32 y = 2;
    ref<i32, shared> r1 = &y;
    ref<i32, shared> r2 = &y;
    i32 i = 0;
    while (i < 3)
    {
        r1 = r2;
        r2 = &x;
        i = i + 1;
    }
    x = 5;
    printf("%v\n", *r1);
}
